# component: message-scroller
# decisions: A11Y-3, A11Y-4, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-9, MOT-5
# hunks:
#   A11Y-3, A11Y-4: NO HUNK, with tests behind both. MEASURED in
#     `@shadcn/react@0.3.1/message-scroller`: `Content` already renders `role="log"` with
#     `aria-relevant="additions"`, and `Viewport` renders `role="region"` with
#     `aria-label="Messages"`. That is A11Y-3 verbatim — a POLITE region by default, announcing
#     added rows rather than every streamed token, and no `alert` anywhere — and A11Y-4's
#     "one mounted-empty region per component" is satisfied by the engine's single `log`: adding
#     a `useAnnouncer` beside it would announce every message twice. `message-scroller.test.tsx`
#     asserts both roles and the `aria-relevant` value, so the day the engine drops them the
#     claim fails instead of going quiet.
#   FOC-9: `MessageScrollerViewport` gains `focus-visible:-outline-offset-2`. The viewport IS a
#     tab stop (the engine gives it `tabIndex={0}`) and `MessageScroller` above it clips with
#     `overflow-hidden`, so `base.css`'s outward `outline-offset: 1px` is drawn and then cut away
#     by the ancestor. FOC-9 is the one permitted local deviation; nothing but the offset moves.
#   MOT-5: `MessageScrollerButton` reads `usePrefersReducedMotion()` and forces the engine's
#     scroll `behavior` to `"auto"`. The engine defaults it to `"smooth"` and knows nothing about
#     the preference, and the global reset in `base.css` cannot reach it — a `scrollTo` that asks
#     for `smooth` explicitly outranks the `scroll-behavior` property — so this wrapper is the
#     only place the preference can be honoured. It overrides whatever the consumer passed, which
#     is what MOT-5 requires ("reduced-motion users get no animation anywhere").
#   A11Y-2: audited, NO HUNK. The one control is `MessageScrollerButton`, which renders a
#     `Button` at `size="icon-sm"` — `size-7`, 28px, over the floor.
#   NOT PATCHED, FLAGGED FOR MK: the engine writes `tabIndex: v ?? 0` on the viewport
#     unconditionally, so a transcript short enough not to scroll is still a tab stop — the half
#     of A11Y-6 Base UI's `ScrollArea.Viewport` gets right. A11Y-6 is not assigned to this
#     component, its second clause licenses a NAMED `role="region"` viewport, and the pre-reset
#     component did not condition it either, so nothing is invented here. The test pins the
#     engine's exact shape so the note fails as stale the day upstream conditions it.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
